{"availability":"available","full":"Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab","name":"CanLab","description":"PyQt6 desktop app for reverse-engineering CAN bus captures. Offline analysis finds counters, checksums and signal boundaries; the DBC builder verifies definitions against real frames; exports DBC, openpilot and Wireshark dissectors. UDS and OBD-II diagnostics. Injection is bench-only and stays disarmed until you arm it.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":86,"forks":9,"created":"2026-04-27T04:47:45Z","updated":"2026-09-23T19:37:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sherin-sef-ai.github.io/CanLab/","topics":["automotive","automotive-security","can-bus","can-fd","canbus","cantools","dbc","groq-api","isotp","j1939","obd2","pyqt6","python","reverse-engineering","socketcan","uds"],"demo":"https://sherin-sef-ai.github.io/CanLab/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.327Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.327Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.327Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.327Z","stars":86,"forks":9}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A desktop workstation for reverse-engineering a CAN bus.","Load a capture, work out which bytes carry what, write the signal definitions down, check them against real frames, and export a DBC that other tools can read. It also speaks the diagnostic protocols (UDS, ISO-TP, J1939, OBD-II, XCP, DoIP), and, for isolated bench use only, can inject, replay, fuzz and bridge.","Status: beta. Single-author project, actively developed. It runs, and the behaviour described here is covered by an automated suite of 578 tests (see Testing). But the analysis methods are heuristics that suggest candidates rather than identify signals, some features need optional dependencies, and it has not been validated across a wide range of real vehicles. Read Limitations before relying on a result."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e3565c58fce59fc14b5491b405faf44c6e3e250411e21dc382918f24db89cced","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.543Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.543Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A desktop workstation for reverse-engineering a CAN bus.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Keys for the optional AI providers go in Settings → API Keys and are stored in the OS keyring; a local Ollama server needs no key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e3565c58fce59fc14b5491b405faf44c6e3e250411e21dc382918f24db89cced","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.544Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T19:37:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/CanLab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:03.547Z","hash":"e3565c58fce59fc14b5491b405faf44c6e3e250411e21dc382918f24db89cced","originalBytes":57029,"storedBytes":57029,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["capture","one","every","frames","core","frame","canlab","against","live","bit","real","bus","which","byte","docs","over","j1939","dbc","each","log","mcp","only","run","what","window","bytes","rather","reference","two","data","python","read","signal","checksum","demo","ids","openpilot","same","through","needs","signals","when","runs","time","detection","does","never","per","python-can","tested","value","message","own","they","tools","uds","command","decoded","http","mark","nmea","other","raw","table","tests","vehicle","adapter","adapters","analysis","both","code","decode","file","gvret","savvycan","test","them","watch","backend","bash","cannot","car","csv","end","install","nothing","opens","pgn","rest","see","speed","under","virtual","across","arm","ba